{"term":"fridge","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:8f3058f1a9f8064967","definition":"A refrigerator.","example":"Sweet broccolini with tofu, sesame, and cilantro […] First, marinate the tofu. In a bowl, whisk the soy sauce, chile sauce, and sesame oil together. Cut the tofu into strips about ⅜ inch / 1 cm thick, mix gently (so it doesn't break) with the marinade, and leave in the fridge for half an hour.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal","wordFamily":["beer fridge","car fridge","fridge-freezer","fridgeful","fridge horror","fridgeless","fridgelike","fridge logic","fridge magnet","microfridge","minifridge","nuke the fridge","poor man's fridge","shut the fridge","upside down fridge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fridge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:51f41ebafb4c056849","definition":"A fat woman.","example":"The fridge protecting the snacks.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet, derogatory, offensive","register":"Internet, derogatory, offensive","wordFamily":["beer fridge","car fridge","fridge-freezer","fridgeful","fridge horror","fridgeless","fridgelike","fridge logic","fridge magnet","microfridge","minifridge","nuke the fridge","poor man's fridge","shut the fridge","upside down fridge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fridge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:52f817d5ff6bdf54f2","definition":"To place (something) inside a refrigerator to chill; to refrigerate.","example":"I had turned up with a bottle, which the hostess, Celia, had duly fridged, but everyone else had opted for camomile tea, making me feel like the biggest lush in south London.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"informal","register":"informal, transitive","wordFamily":["beer fridge","car fridge","fridge-freezer","fridgeful","fridge horror","fridgeless","fridgelike","fridge logic","fridge magnet","microfridge","minifridge","nuke the fridge","poor man's fridge","shut the fridge","upside down fridge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fridge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a835cbbfee6c1e5cb2","definition":"To gratuitously kill, disempower, or otherwise remove (a character, usually female) from a narrative, often strictly to hurt another character (usually male) and motivate vengeance.","example":"The backing cast are also all excellent, as expected considering the calibre of actors attached to the film – Andrea Riseborough is a very good example, playing a fascinating cop who really didn't deserve to be ‘fridged’ (meaning: removed from the action so that the men can do their manly things).","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang, transitive","wordFamily":["beer fridge","car fridge","fridge-freezer","fridgeful","fridge horror","fridgeless","fridgelike","fridge logic","fridge magnet","microfridge","minifridge","nuke the fridge","poor man's fridge","shut the fridge","upside down fridge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fridge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:92924f611631bb0399","definition":"To chafe or rub (something).","example":"A Man's body and his mind, with the utmoſt reverence to both I ſpeak it, are exactly like a jerkin, and a jerkin's lining;—rumple the one—you rumple the other. There is one certain exception however in this caſe, and that is, when you are ſo fortunate a fellow, as to have had your jerkin made of a gum-taffeta, and the body-lining to it, of a ſarcenet or thin perſian. […] [Y]ou might have rumpled and crumpled, and doubled and creaſed, and fretted and fridged the outſides of them all to pieces;—in ſhort, you might have played the very devil with them, and at the ſame time, not one of the inſides of 'em would have been one button the worſe, for all you had done to them.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, archaic, dialectal","register":"UK, archaic, dialectal, transitive","wordFamily":["beer fridge","car fridge","fridge-freezer","fridgeful","fridge horror","fridgeless","fridgelike","fridge logic","fridge magnet","microfridge","minifridge","nuke the fridge","poor man's fridge","shut the fridge","upside down fridge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fridge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:381e2f89a85818efcc","definition":"To chafe or rub.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["beer fridge","car fridge","fridge-freezer","fridgeful","fridge horror","fridgeless","fridgelike","fridge logic","fridge magnet","microfridge","minifridge","nuke the fridge","poor man's fridge","shut the fridge","upside down fridge"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fridge#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a384a533ca3fb5c1cb","definition":"Synonym of fidge (“to jostle or shake; to fidget, to fig, to frig”).","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["fidge"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["beer fridge","car fridge","fridge-freezer","fridgeful","fridge horror","fridgeless","fridgelike","fridge logic","fridge magnet","microfridge","minifridge","nuke the fridge","poor man's fridge","shut the fridge","upside down fridge"],"source":"English Wik